{{infobox entity
 | hidden = yes
 | name   = Poop
 | id     = 245
}}
[[file:Poop.png|54px]]
* Can be destroyed by tears, explosions, stomping effects (such as {{I|Thunder Thighs}}), and certain effects that grant [[invulnerability]] (such as {{i|The Gamekid}} and {{I|My Little Unicorn}}).
* Has a 10% chance to drop a ''pickup'' when destroyed. Of ''those'', 3/4 are [[coin]]s (7.5% of all poops) and 1/4 are [[hearts]] (2.5% of all poops).
* 0.5% or 1/200 poops drop {{t|Petrified Poop}} (if not yet discovered/held).
* Can fill in a gap to create a bridge when pushed in the right direction by an explosion, or by walking into them with {{i|Leo}}/{{i|Thunder Thighs}}.
* If a {{E|Fly}} stays around Poop for long enough, it will morph into a {{E|Pooter}}.

== Corny Poop ==
{{infobox entity
 | hidden = yes
 | name   = Corny Poop
}}
[[file:Corny Poop.png|54px]]
* Has the same chance to drop [[coin]]s, [[heart]]s, and {{t|Petrified Poop}} when destroyed as regular poop.
* Has an {{E|Eternal Fly}} orbiting it that will become an {{E|Attack Fly}} upon destruction of the poop. If Isaac leaves the room without destroying the poop, the orbit of the Eternal Fly will be smaller when he returns.
* {{dlc+|r}} Corny poops thrown by {{c|Tainted ???}} or {{i|IBS}} spawn up to 3 [[Blue Fly|Blue Flies]].{{dlc-}}

== Red Poop ==
{{infobox entity
 | hidden = yes
 | name   = Red Poop
}}
[[file:Red Poop.png|54px]]
* Deals a half-heart of contact damage.
** {{i|Leo}} / {{i|Thunder Thighs}} allows Isaac to walk over and destroy red poop without taking damage. Isaac will still take damage if he is standing on it when it reforms, however.
* Deals 16 contact damage to enemies.
* Drops nothing when destroyed.
* Reforms 3 seconds after being destroyed.
* Normally produced by {{E|Carrion Queen}} and red champion {{E|Dingle}}, but can also be found in specific room configurations in various rooms.
** {{dlc+|a}}In the {{s|Scarred Womb}}, rocks in any room have a chance to be replaced by red poop.{{dlc-}}
** Carrion Queen and red champion Dingle can produce a Red Poop on the [[Boss (Item Pool)|Boss Item]] tile. When the item spawns, the Red Poop will be camouflaged behind the item.
* {{dlc|a}}In some rooms that need to be cleared by pressing silver buttons, red poop will turn into regular poop once all the buttons are pressed.

== Golden Poop ==
{{infobox entity
 | hidden  = yes
 | name    = Golden Poop
 | variant = 1
}}
[[file:Golden Poop.png|54px]]
* Harder to destroy than the normal poop.
* Drops 5-7 [[coin]]s (2/3 chance) or the {{t|Counterfeit Penny}} trinket (1/3 chance) when destroyed.
* If a {{E|Fly}} comes in contact with a Golden Poop, it will turn into a {{E|Pooter}}.
* {{dlc+|anr}} When fighting {{E|Ultra Greed}}, all poop spawned in the boss room will turn into Golden Poop.{{dlc-}}
* {{dlc+|r}} When fighting {{E|Ultra Greed}}, all poop spawned in the boss room will turn into Golden Poop; however, it will not have any of the money-giving effects.{{dlc-}}

== Rainbow Poop ==
{{infobox entity
 | hidden = yes
 | name   = Rainbow Poop
}}
[[file:Rainbow Poop.png|54px]]
* Causes a rainbow to appear on the screen when destroyed; pauses the game for a second while playing a jingle.
* Restores all of Isaac's [[heart container]]s when destroyed, regardless of what destroyed it. Also affects all [[Co-op]] players.
* Rainbow Poop provides no benefit for characters without red heart containers (such as {{c|???}}).
* If a {{E|Fly}} comes in contact with a Rainbow Poop, it will turn into a {{E|Pooter}}.

